  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> be the mid-points of the sides of a triangle with incentre at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math>. If the focus of the parabola <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math> passing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> are rational numbers, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
