  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math> be the mid-points of the sides of a triangle with incentre at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math>,</p><p>Now finding the vertices of the triangle by using midpoint formula and plotting the diagram we get,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8d08a83a-9154-4eb9-9317-7d740b93312b.png\" style=\"width: 306px; height: 197px;\" /></p><p>Now finding the incentre of the above triangle using the formula,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>We get,&nbsp;Incentre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now given parabola&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;passes through the incentre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>D</mi></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Now we know that focus of parabola is given by, focus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Hence, focus will be,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><br />Now comparing with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math><br />Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
